###############################################################################
#  KnowGridFlow / EOIP  —  Logins_credentials.keys
#  Application Security Group (ASG) · Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
#
#  WHAT THIS FILE IS
#  -----------------
#  The single, editable source of truth for who can log into the app and what
#  they are allowed to do. The backend reads this file at startup and builds the
#  ASG token registry. Edit tokens/roles/tenants below and restart the backend
#  (`sudo supervisorctl restart backend`) to apply changes.
#
#  HOW TO LOG IN
#  -------------
#  Open the app, go to the Sign in screen, and paste one of the TOKEN values
#  below into the token field. The role + tenant bound to that token decide what
#  you can see and do. All API calls send it as:  Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>
#
#  APP URLS (replace host with your deployment URL)
#  ------------------------------------------------
#    Sign in ............ /signin
#    Overview ........... /overview
#    Ask (AI) ........... /ask
#    Graph Explorer ..... /graph
#    Meta-graph ......... /meta-graph
#    Time Travel ........ /time
#    Impact ............. /impact
#    Ontology Designer .. /ontology?tab=designer
#    Reports ............ /reports
#    Brand (admin) ...... /brand
#    Governance (admin) . /governance
#    Tenant (admin) ..... /tenant
#
#  ROLES (RBAC MATRIX)
#  -------------------
#    superadmin : FULL CONTROL, CROSS-TENANT. Can do everything, manage every
#                 tenant, publish/rollback ontology, install marketplace packs,
#                 restore/delete snapshots, manage brand, and create/define all
#                 other roles and admins. Implies admin + system. (tenant = *)
#    admin      : Administrative control WITHIN its own tenant. Destructive ops
#                 (ontology publish/merge/rollback, marketplace, snapshots,
#                 ontology import, tenant/brand admin) — scoped to its tenant.
#    system     : Service/automation role (same destructive rights as admin).
#    steward    : Ontology authoring — create drafts, edit, validate, open PRs.
#                 Cannot publish/merge or run destructive admin ops.
#    analyst    : Read + Ask + Impact/Graph exploration + render reports.
#    viewer     : Read-only.
#
#  FAIL-SAFE SUPERADMIN (recovery)
#  -------------------------------
#  There is ALWAYS at least one working superadmin. In addition to the
#  'root-superadmin' entry below, the environment bootstrap token
#  (EOIP_API_TOKEN) is automatically registered as a superadmin even if this
#  file is missing, empty, or has no superadmin — so you can never lock yourself
#  out. The app will not operate without at least one superadmin available.
#
#  SECURITY NOTES
#  --------------
#  * Tokens here are PLAINTEXT for demo/config/troubleshooting convenience.
#  * For production: rotate these values, restrict file permissions (chmod 600),
#    keep it out of public source control, and inject a strong EOIP_API_TOKEN.
#  * Role & tenant boundaries are enforced SERVER-SIDE (not just in the UI).
#
#  ENTRY FORMAT  (pipe-delimited; '#' lines and blank lines are ignored)
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#      <TOKEN> | <role[,role...]> | <tenant | *> | <username>
#
# ===== ASG PRINCIPALS (edit tokens / roles / tenants below) =====

eoip_sa_f86468fed910d947e69eba4c      | superadmin | *       | root-superadmin
eoip_admin_75293814c25a2d4c1e57994c   | admin      | default | default-admin
eoip_steward_449c1099ee3071aa8ce7fbed | steward    | default | data-steward
eoip_analyst_1d0019f09d075ddf8ad141dc | analyst    | default | analyst
eoip_viewer_9072655bae91c450d24fe204  | viewer     | default | viewer

# ===== END ASG PRINCIPALS =====
#
# To ADD a user: copy a line, change the TOKEN (keep it long/random), set role(s)
# and tenant, then restart the backend. To create another tenant's admin, set the
# tenant column to that tenant id (e.g. 'acme') with role 'admin'. Only a
# superadmin may act across tenants.
